Subject: Cantor Candidate Seal and Independent Review Justification

& [JustificationIdentity] is the SJS rationale
  + [justification_uuid] is a4ee370d-631f-428a-a76a-8262db5afeb2
  + [status] is formation_justified_implementation_blocked

& [Problem] is that a mutable candidate and worker testimony cannot prove their own state or correctness
  + [risk] is late mutation, hidden ignored files, incomplete event reporting, self-selected tests, self-review, or implicit promotion
  + [consequence] is unverified code could be mistaken for current authority

& [SelectedSolution] is an immutable evidence pipeline with separate capabilities
  + [Phase3C1] quiesces, reconciles Git and direct bytes, and atomically publishes a content-addressed capture
  + [Phase3C2] reconstructs the sealed source separately and runs only supervisor-authored tests
  + [Phase3C3] independently reviews immutable evidence under deterministic non-waivable gates
  + [Phase3D] alone may later consider promotion

& [WhyNotWorkerReport] is lack of physical authority
  + [worker_report] is useful attributed testimony
  + [failure] is it cannot establish omitted paths, post-report mutations, exact bytes, independent tests, or authority boundaries

& [WhyNotGitOnly] is incomplete physical coverage
  + [value] is base, ref, index, tracked, untracked, ignored, and mode semantics
  + [gap] is physical byte, alias, link, special-file, and consistency assurance
  + [decision] is reconcile Git with a bounded direct inventory

& [WhyNotTestInCandidate] is evidence contamination
  + [risk] is builds and malicious tests mutate the source subject
  + [decision] is seal first and test a deterministic separate reconstruction

& [WhyNotOneProcess] is capability conflation
  + [risk] is capture code can rewrite test evidence, reviewer can access mutable state, or a single success path becomes de facto promotion
  + [decision] is distinct grants, roots, processes, records, and transitions

& [WhyNotImplementNow] is unresolved physical proof
  + [gap] is quiescence, inventory completeness, atomic publication, durability, reconstruction, test containment, and independent-review fixtures
  + [decision] is form CSR-001 through CSR-018 while withholding all effects

& [Rollback] is no runtime change
  + [action] is remove or revise formation documents
  + [preserved] is every proven Cantor interface and Phase3A implementation

& [Decision] is formation accepted and activation rejected
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [live_seal] is blocked
  + [test_execution] is blocked
  + [review_execution] is blocked
  + [promotion] is blocked
